Going forward, please use this as the standard test recipe for every new model. Claude models, meaning Opus and Sonnet, should be tested on both the native Anthropic route and the OpenAI-compatible route, since both are real possibilities for them. All other models, GPT-OSS, Terra, Luna, Gemini, O3, and any others, should be tested on the OpenAI-compatible route only, since native Anthropic isn't a valid route for non-Claude models. For every route you do test, run the same five-part suite, basic inference, a forced tool call, a stateless tool result continuation, a cache-warm request, and an identical replay of that same request to confirm the cache is read back rather than just written. Report raw numbers for each part, not just pass or fail, token counts, the cache creation versus cache read breakdown, and whichever of success or model-not-found actually came back. If a model returns model-not-found, note that explicitly as provisioning-in-progress rather than a final result, and re-test once access should have propagated. This apply at both US and global regions where applicable.
